extends RefCounted
## The political world of 1 January 1590, as data for build_world.gd.
##
## POLITIES: tag -> [name, government, colour ("" = auto), capital [lat, lon]].
## Every capital becomes a forced province seed, so each polity is guaranteed
## its capital province.
##
## RULES: Natural Earth ADM0_A3 code -> who held that land in 1590.
##   "TAG"  the whole modern country belonged to TAG ("" = uncolonised)
##   [default, claim, claim, ...] where a claim is [tag, radius_km, [[lat, lon], ...]].
##   A province takes the claim with the nearest anchor point whose radius
##   reaches it (radius 0 = unlimited). If no claim reaches it, the default
##   applies. All-unlimited claims partition the country by nearest anchor.
##
## Borders are approximations at province resolution, chosen from standard
## historical atlases for 1590. Notable situations encoded here:
##  - Spain and Portugal are in personal union (Iberian Union, 1580) but keep
##    separate crowns and empires.
##  - The Dutch Revolt: the United Provinces hold Holland, Zeeland, Utrecht,
##    Friesland and Breda (taken March 1590); Spain holds Groningen, Zutphen,
##    Deventer, Nijmegen and the south.
##  - France is in its Wars of Religion; Henry IV is king since August 1589.
##  - The Ottoman–Safavid war just ended (Constantinople, 1590): the Ottomans
##    hold Tabriz, Shirvan, Georgia's east and Luristan.
##  - Abdullah Khan II of Bukhara holds Herat (1588) and Mashhad (1589).
##  - Hideyoshi completed the unification of Japan in 1590 (Odawara).
##  - Songhai still stands (the Moroccan invasion comes in 1591).
##  - Russia has just founded Samara (1586), Tsaritsyn (1589), Saratov (1590)
##    and holds Tyumen and Tobolsk; Kuchum's Khanate of Sibir survives east.

